  "worked_solution": "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by applying the inverse Laplace transform to the above result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-2} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\ {e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}} & ={e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the multiplicative property of the inverse Laplace transform, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-2}}=4\\cdot {e}^{2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{s-2}}=4{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
